TAR(1)                      User Commands                    TAR(1)

NAME
    tar - create, list and extract ustar archives

SYNOPSIS
    tar [-C dir] [-z] -c [-v] [-f file] path...
    tar [-C dir] [-z] -t [-v] [-f file]
    tar [-C dir] [-z] -x [-m] [-p] [-v] [-f file] [member...]

DESCRIPTION
    tar writes the named files and directories, recursively, into an
    archive in the ustar format, lists the members of an archive, or
    extracts all or the named members. Without -f the archive is standard
    output for -c and standard input for -t and -x.

OPTIONS
    -c        create an archive from the named paths
    -t        list the members
    -x        extract members
    -f file   use file as the archive
    -C dir    change to dir before reading or writing files
    -z        compress with gzip when creating, decompress when reading;
              gzip runs as a child that tar does not wait for
    -m        give extracted files the current time
    -p        keep the recorded permissions
    -v        print each member name

EXAMPLES
    tar -cf src.tar src
    tar -tzf src.tgz
    tar -C /tmp -xf src.tar src/main.c

SEE ALSO
    ar(1), gzip(1)
